The buttons are now under the cover, centered, wrapping in 2 rows: row 1 = Amazon, Fnac, Kobo; row 2 = Google Books alone. Visually, "Google Books" alone on the second row centered is okay but could be nicer: maybe 2x2 grid would look more balanced. Amazon is wide. Row 1: Amazon + Fnac + Kobo (fits), row 2: Google Books alone. A 2x2 layout (Amazon + Fnac / Kobo + Google) would be more even.

Option: give the buttons a min-width so they wrap evenly, e.g. set .btn-action min-width and flex-basis calc(50% - 10px)? With 4 buttons each ~50% width minus gap, they'd form a 2x2 grid. Amazon button text "Acheter sur Amazon" fits in half width (~180px)? At font 1rem, ~150px text + padding 40 = 190px. Half of wrapper (~423px) minus gap = ~191px. Tight but probably fits; on narrower viewports text could overflow. Safer: flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 10px) with box-sizing... The wrapper width = hero-left width. At 1086 viewport, hero-left ~423px → each ~201px. "Acheter sur Amazon" at 1rem (16px) ≈ 150px + 40 padding = 190. OK.

But at slightly narrower desktop (e.g. 1000px), hero-left ~370px → each 175px → Amazon text wraps to two lines. Hmm. Alternatively keep current wrap behavior which looks decent already. The lone Google Books centered on second row is acceptable, but user asked "Le rendu visuel doit être plaisant" — I can polish: make 2x2 with consistent sizing.

Alternative polish: keep row 1 of three smaller buttons and center Amazon? Eh.

I'll try: .hero-left .btn-action { flex: 1 1 45%; } with min sizing... Actually simpler: .cta-wrapper { max-width: 420px; margin: 0 auto; } and .btn-action { flex: 1 1 40%; } — 2x2 grid, buttons equal width, text centered. Buttons already text-align center. On mobile media query, flex-direction column + width 100% overrides fine.

But .cta-wrapper is also used only in hero-left now. Let me set:

.hero-left .cta-wrapper {
  max-width: 440px;
  margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;
}
.hero-left .btn-action {
  flex: 1 1 180px;
}

flex-basis 180px: wrapper 440 → 2 per row (180*2+20 gap=380 ≤440; 3 per row = 560 > 440). At narrower widths, wraps. Amazon min-content 190px > 180 → row of 2 might overflow? flex-basis 180 but min-width auto → Amazon won't shrink below 190 → row could exceed container? Flex items shrink (flex-shrink default 1) but min-width:auto prevents shrinking below min-content. Container 440 with Amazon(190) + Fnac(~90) = 300 < 440 fine; Kobo joins if 190+90+80+40=... gap 20: 190+20+90+20+80=400 <440 → 3 in a row again! Hmm.

To force 2x2: flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 10px). Then each row has exactly 2 (since two items take 100% minus gap... calc(50% - 10px)*2 + 20 gap = 100%). Items can't fit 3 in a row because each basis is 50%-10. Good, and they stretch to equal widths. Amazon min-content 190 > basis (201 at 423 width)? min-width auto → if min-content > basis, item won't shrink but basis is already 50% of 423 ≈ 201 ≥ 190 fine. At viewport 970 (min desktop ~969): container max 1200, padding 40 each side → hero width = min(1200, 969) - 80 = 889; columns: hero-left = 889 * (1/2.2 gap 60)... flex 1 vs 1.2 with 60 gap: widths ≈ (889-60)*1/2.2=377 and 452. Wrapper = 377 → each button 50%-10 = 178 < 190 → Amazon min-content forces overflow of that row? With flex-wrap and basis 178, Amazon's min 190 → row = Amazon 190 + other 178 + 20 = 388 > 377 → wrap happens: Amazon alone row 1, then Fnac+Kobo row 2, Google alone row 3. Ugly at narrow desktop.

Reduce button padding/font slightly under hero-left? Or set .hero-left .btn-action { font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 10px 14px; white-space: nowrap; } min-content of "Acheter sur Amazon" ≈ 145px text at 0.95rem + 28 = ~173. Container 377 → basis 178 ≥ 173 OK. At 969px works. Below 969 → mobile column anyway.

