- .btn-action font-size smaller: set in .hero-left .btn-action { font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 9px 10px; white-space: nowrap; }
- Remove last-child rule (EN) or keep? With nowrap and flex:1 all equal-ish. Remove the last-child rule in index.html since no longer relevant.
- Remove `flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 10px)` → replace.

Also min-width auto: with nowrap text, min-content per button; total should fit 400. Google Books at 0.9rem (14.4px): ~100px + 20 = 120. OK.

But hero-left column width at narrower desktops (~970px) is ~377px → wrapper 400 max but column only 377 → buttons shrink; with nowrap they might overflow. At 970: available 377; needed ~347 (at gap 10, padding 10) → fits. Good.

Mobile: media query cta-wrapper column + align-items center; .btn-action width 100%, flex 0 0 auto — unchanged. But nowrap + width 100%: text fits, fine. Also .hero-left .btn-action font-size 0.9rem applies on mobile too — buttons slightly smaller text but width 100%. Acceptable; or scope font-size only desktop? Keep simple — mobile buttons full width, 0.9rem text is fine.

