content.text:
The user suggests rethinking the placement — maybe the Google Analytics cookie banner should be full-width on a single line in the footer? Let me redesign:

**Proposal**: 
- The cookie banner becomes a **full-width bar fixed at the very bottom** (like a footer strip): single line, full spread (full width), text left, buttons right — no overlap possible with anything else if the newsletter popup sits ABOVE it.
- The newsletter popup stays bottom-RIGHT but **raised above** the cookie bar height (bottom: e.g. 84px instead of 18px when the bar is present... or always 90px to be safe).

Design: 
```css
#cookie-banner {
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; width: 100%;
  border-radius: 0;
  padding: 14px 30px;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 20px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
```
Single line: text + buttons inline. On mobile: wrap to 2 lines (text on top, buttons below).

And the nl-popup: bottom: 18px → but when the cookie bar is visible (max ~60px tall), the popup would overlap. Two options:
- Since I already made the popup WAIT for the cookie banner to be dismissed, they never coexist ✓ — so the popup can stay at bottom 18px. The waiting logic already handles it!
- But to be extra safe: raise the popup to bottom: 84px always? No — with the wait logic, when the cookie bar shows first and gets dismissed, then the popup appears at bottom 18 ✓ no overlap ever.

So: cookie banner = full-width single-line bottom bar ✓ (the user's suggestion), popup waits ✓ (already done). Redo the CSS on all 6 pages:

```css
    #cookie-banner {
      position: fixed;
      bottom: 0;
      left: 0;
      width: 100%;
      z-index: 200;
      background: rgba(15, 17, 23, 0.98);
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      padding: 14px 30px;
      box-shadow: 0 -10px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
      display: none;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 20px;
      box-sizing: border-box;
      backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    }
```
Remove border-radius, border, transform translateX. Mobile: flex-wrap, column.

The current CSS block (added earlier):
```css
    #cookie-banner {
      position: fixed;
      bottom: 18px;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
      z-index: 200;
      width: min(680px, calc(100% - 30px));
      background: rgba(15, 17, 23, 0.97);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 16px 20px;
      box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
      display: none;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 18px;
      backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    }
```
And the mobile rule:
```css
    @media (max-width: 968px) {
      #cookie-banner { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; text-align: center; }
      .cookie-actions { justify-content: center; }
    }
```
Update mobile: keep column + center.

